# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://dv-flow.github.io/flow.dv.schema.json
package:
  name: fw.hdl.spl
  desc: fw-hdl's steps of the SPL -> RTL pipeline -- partition a structural component, integrate its blocks
  doc: |
    Registered by the fw-hdl Python package (entry point `dv_flow.mgr`), so any
    flow whose Python environment has fw-hdl installed can name these tasks.
    The libproject recipe `project.spl.utils.xls-rtl` wires them to
    `synth.xls.Codegen` and `zuspec.xls.Signature`. See `xls-phase2.md`.

  tasks:
  - name: Partition
    scope: export
    desc: Read a structural fw-hdl component and emit its XLS blocks, plus the shell that integrates them
    doc: |
      Step A of the SPL -> RTL pipeline:

      ```
      Partition ─► xlsIR ─────────────────► synth.xls.Codegen ─► xlsModuleSignature ─┐
                └► blockSignaturePrediction ─────────────────────► zuspec.xls.Signature ─► blockSignature ─┐
                └► splPartition ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────► Integrate ─► systemVerilogSource
      ```

      `top` is a *structural* component: no `run()`, only ports, child
      components and `fw_channel`s (or arrays of them). Its `build()` and
      `connect()` are elaborated, so loops, `if` on parameters and parameter
      objects work. `xls` lists the child classes XLS implements: a class
      name, a typedef naming a specialization, or a generic class (every
      specialization of it). In this release every child must be listed.
      Each distinct child (specialization plus parameter-object values) is
      one block; `partition.json` names it and keeps its SV class as `alias`.

      Each listed class is checked against the static subset here, so an
      unsupported construct is reported on its SV line before any tool runs.

      Outputs:

      * `splPartition` -- `partition.json`: the top's pins, channels,
        children and connections. Integration reads this, not the SV.
      * `xlsIR` -- `<module>.ir` per class (one per class, not per instance).
      * `blockSignaturePrediction` -- `<module>.pred.json` per class: the
        ports XLS codegen is expected to produce with its default naming.

      A module is named after its class: `pkg::cls` becomes `pkg__cls`.
      With an `fwKnobs` input (fw.hdl.knobs.Resolve), each proc channel's
      register comes from the knobs (`xls.chan_flop`, or the block's
      `flop_inputs`/`flop_outputs`): it is written on the IR's
      `chan_interface`, which is where XLS takes it for procs.
    consumes:
    - filetype: systemVerilogSource
    - filetype: verilogSource
    - filetype: fwKnobs
    with:
      top:
        doc: The structural top component (class name or typedef)
        type: str
      xls:
        doc: Child classes to implement with XLS
        type: list
        value: []
    shell: pytask
    run: fw.hdl.dfm_tasks.Partition

  - name: Integrate
    scope: export
    desc: Build the RTL top that instantiates every block and wires its channels
    doc: |
      Step C of the SPL -> RTL pipeline. Reads the `splPartition` shell and one
      `blockSignature` per child module -- never a block's Verilog -- and
      writes a structural top:

      * each child becomes an instance of its block's module;
      * each `fw_channel #(T, DEPTH)` becomes an `fw_rv_fifo` of that width
        and depth (DEPTH 0 is a wire);
      * each of the top's own ports becomes ready/valid pins `<port>`,
        `<port>_vld`, `<port>_rdy`, plus `clk` and `rst`.

      Any block with a `blockSignature` can be integrated. That includes a
      hand-written module: give it a signature file instead of running XLS.

      Outputs:

      * `systemVerilogSource` -- everything to compile, in order: the FIFO,
        each block's module, then the top (fileset param `top`);
      * `blockSignature` -- the top's own signature, so this top can be a
        block of a larger design.
      **Boundary checks**, on each block's Verilog (found through
      its signature's `sources`):

      * no combinational loop through depth-0 channels;
      * no depth-0 channel from a block back to itself;
      * no block output valid that depends combinationally on a ready;
      * every channel between blocks registered in both directions -- a
        FIFO (depth >= 1), or flop-driven valid/data on the producer and
        ready on the consumer -- unless the knobs (`fwKnobs` input) list it in
        `island.exceptions`.

      `boundary` sets the severity of the first three, `registered_boundaries`
      of the last: `error`, `warn` or `off`.
    consumes:
    - filetype: splPartition
    - filetype: blockSignature
    - filetype: fwKnobs
    # The output is exactly the compile list. Passing inputs through would also
    # forward each block's .sv from Codegen, so it would be compiled twice.
    passthrough: none
    with:
      top_name:
        doc: Module name of the top. Default -- the top class's module name.
        type: str
        value: ""
      boundary:
        doc: "Severity of the loop / loopback / valid-on-ready checks: error, warn or off"
        type: str
        value: error
      registered_boundaries:
        doc: "Severity of the registered-both-ways check: error, warn or off"
        type: str
        value: warn
    shell: pytask
    run: fw.hdl.dfm_tasks.Integrate
